    \field{abstract}{%
    Photoelectron spectra are reported for the hydrides of group V and VI elements. Vibrational structure has been observed in bands associated with all but the inner-most valence orbitals. It has been used to obtain changes in bond angles or bond distances which result from the ionization of successive molecular orbitals. Ionization from the inner (1a\textsubscript{1}) orbitals of the hydrides has been observed using He II 304 \AA{} radiation. From these data vertical ionization potentials have been derived for all the valence orbitals of the hydrides XH, XH\textsubscript{2}, XH\textsubscript{3} and XH\textsubscript{4} for which the corresponding united atoms are Ne, A, Kr and Xe. Graphs of these values are used to show the effects of inner shells on the valence orbitals.%
    }
